# What `docker build` may see of the project folder (the "build context").
#
# An allow-list: everything is left out, then the few things the images are built from
# are let back in. The other way round (listing what to leave out) sends any new folder
# to the build by default, and this folder holds 760 MB of data, a model store and a
# Windows virtual environment, none of which belongs in an image. Data and the MLflow
# store reach the containers at run time (bind mounts and the network), never at build
# time. See docker/api.Dockerfile.
#
# This file does not affect the bind mounts of docker-compose.yml: those see the folder
# as it is on disk.

*

# The package: its metadata (pyproject.toml names README.md as its readme, so the build
# needs it) and its source.
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!src/

# The configuration the images carry (the zones, the features, the model parameters).
!configs/

# The lock files the images install from.
!docker/requirements-*.lock

# Python leaves these next to the source when the code is run on this machine.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
